// csv_formula_neutralize: a value whose first non-whitespace character is
// a CSV-formula trigger character (=, +, -, @, a tab, or a carriage
// return) gets a leading single quote prepended, forcing most spreadsheet
// applications to display the whole cell as literal text rather than
// evaluate it as a formula. Defense-in-depth against CWE-1236 -- see this
// op's own docstring for its documented scope/limits.
